cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its experimental data, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Ascend-FFT: A Hardware-Mapped FFT Operator Library for Huawei Ascend NPUs"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Teng"
    family-names: "Wang"
    email: "wangt635@ustc.edu.cn"
    affiliation: "High Efficient Intelligent Computing Lab, Suzhou Institute for Advanced Research of USTC, Suzhou, China"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TruNcat3/ascend-fft"
url: "https://github.com/TruNcat3/ascend-fft"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
abstract: >-
  A hardware-mapped FFT operator library and reproducible research artifact
  for Huawei Ascend NPUs. It applies the cuButterfly space-time mapping method
  through target-specific AscendC processing units, memory movement, legality
  checks, cost modeling, and measured plan selection. The current release
  validates fp32 C2C, R2C, and C2R paths on Ascend910_9382 while retaining an
  extensible design space for additional numeric and transform contracts.
keywords:
  - FFT
  - Ascend
  - AscendC
  - NPU
  - FFT operator library
  - hybrid dataflow
  - cost model
  - design space search
  - space-time parallelism
references:
